nication, participant connection records, audio/video, file and screen sharing, and learning platforms capable of supporting collaborative work and tracking participation.</p>
  <p class="footer">IFCD104 · Unofficial English translation for portfolio review</p>
</section>

<section class="page">
  <h2>Online-learning platform requirements</h2>
  <h3>Infrastructure</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Capacity and server response appropriate to the enrolled learner population and concurrent usage.</li>
    <li>Bandwidth sufficient for real-time audiovisual communication; the source syllabus specifies a minimum server bandwidth of 300 Mbps.</li>
    <li>24/7 platform availability.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Software and interoperability</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Compatibility with SCORM and IMS content packages.</li>
    <li>Web accessibility/interactivity aligned with the applicable Spanish accessibility standard cited in the source syllabus.</li>
    <li>Compliance with applicable Spanish and EU data-protection requirements, including the GDPR framework where relevant.</li>
    <li>Compatibility with common operating systems, databases, browsers and web servers.</li>
    <li>Operational training-tracking web services in accordance with the applicable data model/protocol cited by the source syllabus.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Services and learner support</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Host the complete virtual learning material for the training specialty.</li>
    <li>Provide centralised technical support throughout the training action.</li>
    <li>Support synchronous and asynchronous communication, including messaging, forums and chat.</li>
    <li>Support group collaboration, user/permission management, content management, assessment, grading and learner-progress tracking.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Virtual learning materials</h3>
  <p>Materials must address the programme's objectives and learning outcomes, be pedagogically structured, encourage practical application, use relevant multimedia/interactive resources, support supplementary resources and glossaries, and include formative and final assessment activities.</p>
  <p class="footer">IFCD104 · Unofficial English translation for portfolio review</p>
</section>

